, is_editable=False, is_enabled=True, is_focused=False, is_focusable=False, is_long_clickable=False, is_scrollable=False, is_selected=False, is_visible=True, package_name='com.android.systemui', resource_name='com.android.systemui:id/battery', tooltip=None, resource_id=None, metadata=None)\\n\\nThis is the action you picked: {\\\"action_type\\\": \\\"click\\\", \\\"index\\\": 4}\\nBased on the reason: The minute picker shows 45 is selected (checked). I need to click OK to confirm the end time of 06:45.\\n\\n\\nBy comparing the descriptions for the two screenshots and the action performed, give a brief summary of this step. This summary will be added to action history and used in future action selection, so try to include essential information you think that will be most useful for future action selection like what you intended to do, why, if it worked as expected, if not what might be the reason (be critical, the action/reason might not be correct), what should/should not be done next and so on. Some more rules/tips you should follow:\\n- Keep it short and in one line.\\n- Some actions (like `answer`, `wait`) don't involve screen change, you can just assume they work as expected.\\n- Given this summary will be added into action history, it can be used as memory to include information that needs to be remembered, or shared between different apps.\\n\\nSummary of this step: \"\nevidence/native_run/trajectories/steps.json:33055:    \"action_output\": \"Reason: All fields are correctly set: title \\\"Meeting with Bob\\\", description, date October 16 (Mon), start time 06:00, end time 06:45. Now I need to click Save to create the event.\\n\\nAction: {\\\"action_type\\\": \\\"click\\\", \\\"index\\\": 2}\",\nevidence/native_run/trajectories/steps.json:33056:    \"action_prompt\": \"You are an agent who can operate an Android phone on behalf of a user. Based on user's goal/request, you may\\n- Answer back if the request/goal is a question (or a chat message), like user asks \\\"What is my schedule for today?\\\".\\n- Complete some tasks described in the requests/goals by performing actions (step by step) on the phone.\\n\\nWhen given a user request, you will try to complete it step by step. At each step, a list of descriptions for most UI elements on the current screen will be given to you (each element can be specified by an index), together with a history of what you have done in previous steps. Based on these pieces of information and the goal, you must choose to perform one of the action in the following list (action description followed by the JSON format) by outputing the action in the correct JSON format.\\n- If you think the task has been completed, finish the task by using the status action with complete as goal_status: `{\\\"action_type\\\": \\\"status\\\", \\\"goal_status\\\": \\\"complete\\\"}`\\n- If you think the task is not feasible (including cases like you don't have enough information or can not perform some necessary actions), finish by using the `status` action with infeasible as goal_status: `{\\\"action_type\\\": \\\"status\\\", \\\"goal_status\\\": \\\"infeasible\\\"}`\\n- Answer user's question: `{\\\"action_type\\\": \\\"answer\\\", \\\"text\\\": \\\"<answer_text>\\\"}`\\n- Click/tap on a UI element (specified by its index) on the screen: `{\\\"action_type\\\": \\\"click\\\", \\\"index\\\": <target_index>}`.\\n- Long press on a UI element (specified by its index) on the screen: `{\\\"action_type\\\": \\\"long_press\\\", \\\"index\\\": <target_index>}`.\\n- Type text into an editable text field (specified by its index), this action contains clicking the text field, typing in the text and pressing the enter, so no need to click on the target field to start: `{\\\"action_type\\\": \\\"input_text\\\", \\\"text\\\": <text_input>, \\\"index\\\": <target_index>}`\\n- Press the Enter key: `{\\\"action_type\\\": \\\"keyboard_enter\\\"}`\\n- Navigate to the home screen: `{\\\"action_type\\\": \\\"navigate_home\\\"}`\\n- Navigate back: `{\\\"action_type\\\": \\\"navigate_back\\\"}`\\n- Scroll the screen or a scrollable UI element in one of the four directions, use the same numeric index as above if you want to scroll a specific UI element, leave it empty when scroll the whole screen: `{\\\"action_type\\\": \\\"scroll\\\", \\\"direction\\\": <up, down, left, right>, \\\"index\\\": <optional_target_index>}`\\n- Open an app (nothing will happen if the app is not installed): `{\\\"action_type\\\": \\\"open_app\\\", \\\"app_name\\\": <name>}`\\n- Wait for the screen to update: `{\\\"action_type\\\": \\\"wait\\\"}`\\n\\nThe current user goal/request is: In Simple Calendar Pro, create a calendar event for this Monday at 6h with the title 'Meeting with Bob' and the description 'We will understand annual budget. Remember to confirm attendance.'. The event should last for 45 mins.\\n\\nHere is a history of what you have done so far:\\nStep 1: Action selected: {\\\"action_type\\\": \\\"open_app\\\", \\\"app_name\\\": \\\"Simple Calendar Pro\\\"}. Opened Simple Calendar Pro app; now on the October month view. Need to tap the \\\"New Event\\\" FAB (bottom right) to start creating the event for this Monday at 6:00 with title \\\"Meeting with Bob\\\".\\nStep 2: Action selected: {\\\"action_type\\\": \\\"click\\\", \\\"index\\\": 6}. Tapped the \\\"New Event\\\" FAB which expanded to show \\\"Event\\\" and \\\"Task\\\" options; I need to click \\\"Event\\\" (index 9) next to open the event creation screen.\\nStep 3: Action selected: {\\\"action_type\\\": \\\"click\\\", \\\"index\\\": 9}. Clicked \\\"Event\\\" (index 9) from the FAB menu to open the New Event creation screen; it worked as expected - now showing form with Title, Location, Description fields, start/end date of \\\"October 15 (Sun)\\\" at 16:00. Need to set title, description, change date to this Monday, time to 06:00, and end time to 06:45.\\nStep 4: Action selected: {\\\"action_type\\\": \\\"input_text\\\", \\\"text\\\": \\\"Meeting with Bob\\\", \\\"index\\\": 4}. Entered \\\"Meeting with Bob\\\" in the Title field successfully; next need to enter the description, set start date to this Monday, start time to 6:00, and end time to 6:45.\\nStep 5: Action selected: {\\\"action_type\\\": \\\"input_text\\\", \\\"text\\\": \\\"We will understand annual budget. Remember to confirm attendance.\\\", \\\"index\\\": 7}. Entered the description \\\"We will understand annual budget. Remember to confirm attendance.\\\" into the Description field (index 7); it worked as the field now shows the text. Next, I need to set the start date to this Monday, start time to 06:00, and end time to 06:45 (45 min duration).\\nStep 6: Action selected: {\\\"action_type\\\": \\\"click\\\", \\\"index\\\": 8}. Clicked on the start date field (\\\"October 15 (Sun)\\\") to open the date picker; the date picker dialog is now showing with Oct 15, 2023 selected. Next, I should tap on Oct 16 (Monday) and confirm with OK to set the start date.\\nStep 7: Action selected: {\\\"action_type\\\": \\\"click\\\", \\\"index\\\": 22}. Clicked on Oct 16 in the date picker to select \\\"this Monday\\\"; header now shows \\\"Mon, Oct 16\\\" confirming the date is selected. Next, I need to click OK to confirm the date.\\nStep 8: Action selected: {\\\"action_type\\\": \\\"click\\\", \\\"index\\\": 6}. Clicked OK to confirm date selection (Mon, Oct 16, 2023) in the date picker. The event editor now shows the date correctly set to \\\"October 16 (Mon)\\\" with title \\\"Meeting with Bob\\\" and description already filled in. Still need to change start time from 16:00 to 06:00 and end time to 06:45 (for 45 min duration), then save.\\nStep 9: Action selected: {\\\"action_type\\\": \\\"click\\\", \\\"index\\\": 8}. Clicked the start time field (showing 16:00) to open the time picker dialog so I can change the start time to 06:00; the time picker opened successfully with 16 hours currently selected - next I need to select 6 (for 6h/06:00) and confirm with OK.\\nStep 10: Action selected: {\\\"action_type\\\": \\\"click\\\", \\\"index\\\": 25}. Clicked on \\\"6\\\" in the hour clock face to set the start hour to 6; the picker now shows hour as \\\"06\\\" and advanced to the minute selection view (00 minutes selected). Next, keep minutes at 00 and click OK to confirm 6:00 start time.\\nStep 11: Action selected: {\\\"action_type\\\": \\\"click\\\", \\\"index\\\": 4}. Clicked OK to confirm the start time of 06:00 on Monday October 16; returned to the New Event screen showing title, description, and start/end times both at 06:00 \\u2014 still need to change end time to 06:45.\\nStep 12: Action selected: {\\\"action_type\\\": \\\"click\\\", \\\"index\\\": 10}. Clicked on end time field (06:00) to open the time picker; a clock dial time picker appeared with 06 hours selected. Next, I need to change minutes to 45 by clicking the minute field and selecting 45, then tap OK.\\nStep 13: Action selected: {\\\"action_type\\\": \\\"click\\\", \\\"index\\\": 1}. Clicked on the \\\"00\\\" minute field to switch the time picker from hour selection to minute selection; the picker now shows minute options (00, 05, 10, ..., 55), and I should next click \\\"45\\\" to set the minutes.\\nStep 14: Action selected: {\\\"action_type\\\": \\\"click\\\", \\\"index\\\": 10}. Clicked \\\"45\\\" in the minute picker to set end time minutes to 45; the minute display now shows 45 as selected, so end time is now 06:45 (45 minutes after 06:00 start). Next, click OK to confirm the end time.\\nStep 15: Action selected: {\\\"action_type\\\": \\\"click\\\", \\\"index\\\": 4}. Clicked OK to confirm the end time picker with 06:45 selected. The event form now shows start time 06:00 and end time 06:45 on October 16 (Mon), with title and description already filled. Next step is to click Save to create the event.\\n\\nHere is a list of descriptions for some UI elements on the current screen:\\nUI element 0: UIElement(text=None, content_description=None, clas